WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.486
- But here's what's good about 30

00:00:01.486 --> 00:00:03.226
is that you drink through your mouth

00:00:03.226 --> 00:00:08.173
instead of pouring alcohol
into a funnel into your butt.

00:00:08.173 --> 00:00:09.963
(laughter)

00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:12.753
That's the new craze.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.725
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:22.553
- I don't consider 30 old, per say,

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:24.573
I consider it on the way up.

00:00:24.573 --> 00:00:28.497
- 30 is midlife crisis and
then you find yourself.

00:00:28.497 --> 00:00:30.355
- When I hear the age
30 I think of better,

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.003
you know, more wisdom.

00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:34.604
- I don't, I don't want to be 30.

00:00:34.604 --> 00:00:36.834
- It seems old, it does.
- 30 seems old.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:37.761
- It does.

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:39.295
- I know.
(cries)

00:00:39.295 --> 00:00:40.107
- It's okay.

00:00:40.107 --> 00:00:42.011
That's the scary part,
is that you go to bed 29,

00:00:42.011 --> 00:00:44.983
you wake up 30 and it's the same life.

00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:46.747
- Everyone said midlife
crises, that's not...

00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:49.626
- Yeah, that's the weird ones.

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:51.043
- It's funny, what they don't realize is

00:00:51.043 --> 00:00:52.482
that the quarter-life crisis I feel like

00:00:52.482 --> 00:00:54.732
is actually pretty true.

00:00:54.732 --> 00:00:56.876
You get out of college
and then you're like. . .

00:00:56.876 --> 00:00:58.766
- [Man] What am I doing with my life.

00:00:58.766 --> 00:00:59.734
- [Woman] "oh shit."

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.164
- I think the quarter-life crisis is just

00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:02.488
you have to pay rent.

00:01:02.488 --> 00:01:06.853
- Parties will be irrelevant
because I'll be too old.

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:08.455
- The parties will be ending early.

00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:09.408
- Parties will be boring.

00:01:09.408 --> 00:01:10.940
30-year-olds just drink wine

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.053
and let's have a night watching SVU.

00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:16.327
- Parties at 30 actually get a lot better.

00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:17.069
- Yeah

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:18.462
- Because the parties
that you're going to now

00:01:18.462 --> 00:01:20.297
are just loud music and skunk beer.

00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:21.992
- Oh, and sweat

00:01:21.992 --> 00:01:23.338
- And sweat.
- And shame.

00:01:23.338 --> 00:01:24.732
- Maybe this is good
or bad but I still host

00:01:24.732 --> 00:01:26.544
a lot of parties that go 'till 4 am.

00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:29.282
- Where did you get that we
all drink wine all the time?

00:01:29.282 --> 00:01:30.861
- I've had wine before.

00:01:30.861 --> 00:01:33.137
- Wine will become your
best friend in your thirties

00:01:33.137 --> 00:01:34.669
if maybe ditched the boxed wine.

00:01:34.669 --> 00:01:36.225
- When you leave the party's over.

00:01:36.225 --> 00:01:38.454
So it doesn't really
matter what time it is.

00:01:38.454 --> 00:01:39.645
- When I leave.

00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:43.214
- Hopefully boys will be
men by the time they're 30.

00:01:43.214 --> 00:01:44.143
(laughter)

00:01:44.143 --> 00:01:45.746
That's gonna be the best, or not.

00:01:45.746 --> 00:01:47.766
I mean, maybe they need to
be, like, 35, I don't know.

00:01:47.766 --> 00:01:50.203
- I feel like by the time I
turn 30 I really wouldn't care

00:01:50.203 --> 00:01:52.316
what people think, at all.

00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:54.374
- Depending on how cool my twenties are,

00:01:54.374 --> 00:01:55.801
maybe I'll be married.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:58.491
- But nobody will know
that I am 30, when I'm 30.

00:01:58.491 --> 00:01:59.814
Everyone's gonna think I'm still 29.

00:01:59.814 --> 00:02:01.997
- Like right now I'm still
kind of in that teenage mindset

00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:04.387
where I feel that
everyone's criticizing me

00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:07.450
- But when I'm 30, I just wanna live.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.967
- We'll be the wine-night
30-year-olds who are like,

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:10.824
"Ugh, those 20-year-olds don't
know what they're doing."

00:02:10.824 --> 00:02:12.265
- Uh-huh, but they sure are hot.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.542
(laughter)

00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:15.748
- The only thing that
I've learned from 20 to 30

00:02:15.748 --> 00:02:17.838
is that I don't know anything.

00:02:17.838 --> 00:02:19.881
Once you realize that you don't know shit,

00:02:19.881 --> 00:02:22.040
- Then you know shit.
- Then you know shit.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.271
- Yeah, you definitely come into your own

00:02:23.271 --> 00:02:26.313
and you feel so much more
comfortable just being yourself.

00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:29.331
- If you think that women are
gonna get better by the time

00:02:29.331 --> 00:02:31.514
they're 30, just wait 'till
you have a 40-year-old.

00:02:31.514 --> 00:02:34.811
- The answer is you're not gonna
be where you think you are.

00:02:34.811 --> 00:02:37.713
- Yeah. Totes.
- Deep.

00:02:37.713 --> 00:02:39.083
(laughter)

00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:40.569
- [voiceover] There's one
last thing I'd like to say:

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:43.448
fireball is--
- [ Man in hat] Delicious.

00:02:43.448 --> 00:02:45.343
- [Man with beard] Awful.
- [Man in hat] Oh.

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:48.208
- None of these fools know what the f***

00:02:48.208 --> 00:02:50.155
they're talking about.

